menu "ESP32 AdBlocker Reborn"

    choice ADBLOCK_BOARD
        prompt "Target board"
        default ADBLOCK_BOARD_T_ETH_ELITE
        help
            Selects the W5500 + SD-card pin map compiled into the firmware,
            and the mDNS hostname (esp32adblock.local for the Elite,
            esp32adblock2.local for the Waveshare, so two units can share a
            LAN). Both Ethernet boards are ESP32-S3 with 16MB flash + 8MB
            octal PSRAM, so everything else is identical. NOTE: a web-UI OTA
            upload of the wrong board's image leaves Ethernet dead until
            the rollback watchdog reverts it — flash the matching build.

            The generic Wi-Fi-only target (#49) compiles out the W5500
            driver, the L2 Ethernet fast path and the SD card entirely, so
            the sinkhole runs on any plain ESP32-S3 dev board over its
            built-in Wi-Fi: same DNS engine, blocklist, cache, web UI and
            OTA, minus the Ethernet-only latency offload and the SD
            instant-boot (the blocklist downloads on each cold boot).

        config ADBLOCK_BOARD_T_ETH_ELITE
            bool "LilyGO T-ETH-Elite (W5500 on 48/47/21/45)"

        config ADBLOCK_BOARD_WAVESHARE_S3_ETH
            bool "Waveshare ESP32-S3-ETH (W5500 on 13/12/11/14)"

        config ADBLOCK_BOARD_GENERIC_S3_WIFI
            bool "Generic ESP32-S3 dev board (Wi-Fi only — no W5500, no SD card)"
            select ADBLOCK_NET_WIFI
    endchoice

    config ADBLOCK_NET_ETH
        bool
        default y if !ADBLOCK_BOARD_GENERIC_S3_WIFI
        default n
        help
            Derived, not user-set: the board has a W5500 Ethernet controller
            (and an SD slot). Gates the esp_eth bring-up, the L2 RX fast-path
            hook and the SD mount in dns_sink.cpp.

    config ADBLOCK_NET_WIFI
        bool "Compile in Wi-Fi STA support alongside W5500 Ethernet (dual-WAN)" if ADBLOCK_NET_ETH
        default n
        help
            Whether Wi-Fi STA support is compiled into this image at all —
            NOT whether it's actually brought up at boot. Join a Wi-Fi network
            in addition to the W5500 Ethernet link, so both are up at once —
            e.g. answer LAN DNS queries on Ethernet while egressing upstream
            resolver queries out Wi-Fi (or vice versa), useful when the two
            links sit behind different ISPs/NAT. Which interface egresses
            upstream is chosen at runtime from the web UI (persisted in NVS).
            SD card, blocklist, DNS server, and web UI are unchanged. The L2
            fast-path RX hook is Ethernet-only; Wi-Fi-egressed queries take
            the normal lwIP socket path.

            Whether it's actually enabled is now a runtime NVS flag, toggled
            from the web UI's Network tab (reboot to apply) — no reflash
            needed to switch between single- and dual-WAN once a build has
            this compiled in. On first boot (no NVS value yet) it's seeded
            enabled — the only state this code can seed, since it only exists
            when this option is y — so upgrading an existing dual-WAN board
            doesn't silently drop Wi-Fi. SSID/
            password below are still compile-time only as a first-boot seed —
            set from the web UI (or the USB console's `wifi` command)
            afterwards, same as before.

            Forced on (and the only link, not user-toggleable) for the
            generic Wi-Fi-only board.

    config ADBLOCK_WIFI_SSID
        string "Wi-Fi SSID"
        depends on ADBLOCK_NET_WIFI
        default ""

    config ADBLOCK_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "Wi-Fi password"
        depends on ADBLOCK_NET_WIFI
        default ""

endmenu
